# GoGo-BE code owners.
#
# Declarative: `develop` protection has `require_code_owner_reviews: false` and
# 0 required approvals (owner decision 2026-09-15, `git.md` — a single
# collaborator cannot approve their own pull request, so enforcing it would
# deadlock every merge). GitHub therefore suggests these reviewers rather than
# demanding them; the rule that the owner signs these paths is in `git.md`, and
# this file is what makes "which paths" readable in the repository instead of
# only in a rules file.
#
# Raised by Sol as GoGo-BE#703 F-03 — a pull request that only edits the
# breaking-change policy was invisible to any ownership check.

# Everything, unless a later rule wins.
*                                   @namnh92

# The published contract. Consumers vendor this and generate clients from it.
/openapi/                           @namnh92

# The breaking-change policy itself: the recorded exceptions, the script that
# judges oasdiff's report, and the workflow that wires them together.
/.github/oasdiff-exceptions.json    @namnh92
/scripts/check-contract-compat.ts   @namnh92
/scripts/check-openapi-version.ts   @namnh92
/.github/workflows/                 @namnh92

# The rest of what `git.md` names: schema, authentication, permissions, ranking.
# Paths verified against the tree — migrations live at the repository root, and
# authentication is `identity`, not `auth`.
/migrations/                        @namnh92
/libs/database/                     @namnh92
